{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503706-chicago-1871","id":1503706,"title":"Chicago 1871","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-22T16:54:44-08:00","id":1503706,"title":"Chicago 1871","content":"Back in 2020 I was running a Chicago game that would flashback between modern nights and from the 1860s onward. We explored 1863 and 1925 before going on hiatus. Now I am bringing the game back, starting in 1871 before the Great Chicago Fire. I am looking to populate kindred society. Does anyone have any suggestions on kindred from other books besides Chicago by Night that might be present in 1871? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:56:25-08:00","id":1503779,"title":"","content":"On top of my mind<ul><li>Yaryan</li> <li>Menelao</li> <li>Helena</li> <li>Maria</li> <li>Anabelle Triabell</li> <li>Nicolai Antonescu</li> <li>Mauren Oleary</li> <li>Lodin</li> <li>Ventrues that Lodin later exterminated</li> <li>Maxwell</li> <li>Maxwell allies and progeny</li> </ul>Take in mind that in mind that 1857 Chicago would not have such a big numbers of vampires as in the 90s or 2000s. Vampire population growth often follows the growth of the human population,<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T23:20:25-08:00","id":1503793,"title":"","content":"Maria and Anabelle have a contradictory write up in CbN. While in Anabelle's description is said that they arrived to Chicago at the height of the Jazz Age, Elzbieta's backstory tells us she fought out Anabelle in 1889. In my Chicago game I reconciled this by stating that Maria and her Childe visited that year but moved on, only returning in the 1920's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T01:24:59-08:00","id":1503794,"title":"","content":"Inyanga's write up in CbN establishes that she arrived to Chicago in 1852 and made it her home, but also that she travels a lot across the American continent. She was also a supporter of Maxwell. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bWhen I created my timeline for my CbN game I decided that she was out of town during the events of the Great Fire, otherwise Lodin wouldn't have dared to attack Maxwell. When she came back she disliked the new situation but couldn't do much about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T01:28:12-08:00","id":1503795,"title":"","content":"CbN establishes Drummond's Embrace date at 1865, which is likely a mistake, but I think it would be great to include him. II would tone down his silly vibe and make him a more competent, if ultimately weak, crony of Lodin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T11:26:36-08:00","id":1503830,"title":"","content":"My game actually has a PC grandchilde of Annabelle and PC childe of Lodin. In the 1863 storyline I had Annabelle and Maria traveling through Chicago. Lodin and his childe actually arrived in Chicago then as well. The PC childe took the spot as first of Lodin\u2019s two broods. The main arc of the 1871 storyline will be Lodin taking the city, potentially with the PC coterie\u2019s help.<br /> <br /> I agree with suggestions of which Chicago characters were likely present in 1871.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the conversation about the whereabouts of Chicago characters but I was hoping more for suggestions of other VtM characters it might make sense to be in the city circa 1871. For example, does it make sense to have Hrolulf of Milwaukee visiting Chicago at this time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T20:34:03-08:00","id":1504530,"title":"","content":"I've been big on post-bellum America 1860 to 1900's, mostly because I have a cool map-making program that has tile-sets of buildings of that era; I've read Chicago by Night, and I liked it at first, but, at the time, I didn't like the NPCs in the books. So, I'd suggest making a whole new cast of NPC's for 1871; Vampires do move around a bit. I was always making my own NPCs and not using the books, so it's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}